Good morning from the Rochester Daily.

Here are three local stories making waves around our city today:

1. Downtown Revitalization: City planners have announced a new initiative to convert vacant industrial spaces near the inner loop into mixed-use artist studios and community galleries, aiming to boost local creative energy.
2. Public Parks Update: Highland Park is gearing up for its annual autumn planting drive, looking for volunteers to help prep the soil for spring tulip bulbs.
3. Local Food Scene: A popular neighborhood bakery on Park Avenue is expanding its weekend hours to accommodate growing demand for their sourdough pastries.

